menu "Audio"

config AUDIO_CAPTURE
    bool "Audio capture producer (AMIC/DMIC/I2S) with multicast"
    default n
    help
      Enable audio_capture framework: DMA-driven mic capture (analog mic,
      PDM digital mic, or I2S) with multi-consumer StreamBuffer multicast.
      Consumers: audio recorders, STT, UAC loopback, voice assistant, etc.

config AUDIO_OUTPUT
    bool "Audio output sink abstraction (DAC/UAC/I2S/DUMP)"
    default n
    help
      Enable audio_output framework: pluggable PCM sink with DAC backend
      (one-shot + N-ring streaming), UAC backend, I2S backend, and raw
      dump backend (file or custom hook). Includes linear resampler.

config AUDIO_OUTPUT_UAC_EXCLUDE
    bool "Do not build the UAC output backend"
    depends on AUDIO_OUTPUT
    default n
    help
      Leave audio_output_uac.c out of the build even when
      CHERRYUSB_DEVICE_AUDIO is on.

      Required by any app that implements its own USB Audio Class device —
      a microphone, for instance. usbd_audio_open(), usbd_audio_close() and
      usbd_audio_in_callback() are fixed-name callbacks of the CherryUSB
      audio class, so the backend and an app-side implementation collide at
      link time ("multiple definition").

      Opt-out rather than opt-in so apps that do not set it keep building
      the backend exactly as before.

endmenu
